  <p>You staying here means curiosity has won today! Let's dive!</p>



  <h2>Why yet another popover implementation?</h2>
  <p>If you have been doing frontend for a while you might have noticed there are tons of popover/tooltips
    implementations. Sometimes they work, sometimes they render off the screen, sometimes styling is limited. Yet the
    biggest issue is their performance. Reacting to changes in layout and keep recalculating a position in JS might not
    seem
    like a lot. The situation quickly changes if you have a list, table or just lots of buttons with tooltips. Suddenly
    your
    10ms spend on just attaching listeners and using <a
      href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Element/getBoundingClientRect" target="_blank">Bounding
      box</a>/<a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/ResizeObserver"
      target="_blank">ResizeObserver</a> to calculate initial position grows to 1 second! Doesn't it sound silly?
    Slowing down the app due to something that trivial like tooltips?</p>

