  <a-h2 content="New Popover API" />
  <p>New popover API arrived, it's baseline 2024 newly available. It can be used for tooltips, popovers and modals as
    well! It leverages the power of CSS and HTML to provide stunning user experience without a need for JavaScript
    library. Lack of Javascript allows your business logic to do not compete with tooltips for computing
    power of single tthreaded JS.</p>

  <p>That's all sound good but... creating a popover is not that trivial, even with new API, you have to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Be aware of containin block & inset-modified containing block to know how to correctly position popover</li>
    <li>Ensure the trigger can be used as popover anchor. They both have to live in same containg block and
      same DOM tree</li>
    <li>Handle various edge cases with positioning tooltip when the space is limited.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>That's why today we gonna take a look at implementation that should work in (hopefully) all cases.</p>


  <h3>What exactly new API gives us?</h3>
  <p>We have received plenty of new tools to play with. The ones we are going to use today are:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      HTML attribute <code>Popover</code>- an attribute on popover to indicate the behaviour. Three values allowed
      <code>auto</code>(default), <code>hint</code> and <code>manual</code>. First two can dismisse popover by clicking
      outside the popvoer area or pressing Esc, last one require manual click on tirgger/closing button to dismiss.
      General difference between <code>auto</code> and code>hint</code> is that opening popvoer with type
      <code>auto</code> closes other
      popover with type <code>auto</code> and opening popover with type <code>hint</code> closes other popovers with
      type
      <code>hint</code>, unless popovers are nested!. <a
        href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Global_attributes/popover">Read more on
        MDN.</a>
    </li>
    <li>
      HTML attribute <code>popovertarget</code> - Turn a button into trigger for a popover. This attibute expect id of
      the popover as
      the
      value. Read more on <a
        href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Elements/button#popovertarget"
        target="_blank">MDN</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      CSS rule <code>position-anchor</code> - allows to position the popover relative to the desired element/trigger.
      Along with that new CSS math function can be used <code>anchor()</code> which accept <code>inset</code>
      properties(<code>top</code>, <code>right</code>, <code>bottom</code>, <code>left</code>) and return
      <code>length</code> value.
    </li>
    <li>
      CSS rule <code>anchor-name</code> - allows an element to be used as an anchor for popover positioning.
    </li>
  </ul>

